{"text": "From: Nelson, Byron (WKA)\nTo: Anderson, Doug (WKA); Brinkley, Carolyn G.; Cockman, Michael; Cole, Ron W.;\nCook, Bruce A.; Cruz, Cynthia; Ellis, Jim W.; Goodyear, Douglas; Holland, Toussaint Le;\nHyde, Timothy N.; Klein, Chery! (WKA); Klein, Walt (WKA); Lester, Frank G,; Loeser,\nGary; Marshall, M. Hurst; Morrow, John (WKA); Mozingo, Roger L.; Murray, Joc S.;\nPhillips, Mike W.; Powers, David M.; Shore, Pat J.; Singleton, John W.; Smith, Mark D.;\nStokes, Henry S.; Suggs, Michael L.; Tompson, Randy; Williams, Richard L.; Wold,\nKent L.; \u2018Shad Foos\u2019; \u2018Matt Tilley\u2019\nCC: Fox, William; Milder, Ally; Mitchell, Susan\nBCC:\nPrimary Date: 2/28/1997 PM\nLast Modified Date: 2001-Nov-20 14:56:36\nLast Touched Date:\nSent Date: 1997-Feb-28 08\nReceived Date: 1997-Feb-28 13\nSubject: Moming Team Notes\n\nMorning Team Notes 3/3 Date: 2/28/97\nMaine~-Kent Wold requests direct conncet calls to several key senators and keeping up\ncalls to House members in order to help stop L211 which would undo sales pre-emption\nstatewide. The bill is still in the Senate awaiting an amendment vote on Tuesday before\npethaps going over to the House.\n\nUtah--Henry Stokes requests direct connect calls to key House members either at their\nistrict office number or at their residence hotel in Salt Lake City. House members will\nbe urged to vote against the bill which would ban smoking in condos, even privately\nowned condos if smoke drifts into other parts of the building.\n\nNebraska--On 3/12, the Judiciary Committee will hold a hearing on L158 which would\nban the self-service displays of tobacco products at relail. A hearing on the 10-cent per\npack tax hike was help 2/28. We are awaiting words on any grassroots action from\nretailers,\n\nRJR0000000508022478\n\n70018 0873\n\nlesz Loses",
